column3:
Daily fixture manager update: reserve fixtures, queued fixture news, removal of AI-only friendlies and cup round labels. 
 `FIXTURE_MANAGER::daily_update()`, from the day loop (0x5cc850); SEH frame with no destructor on the normal path (the local dates). By today's weekday (0x54a3f0 on 0xae2c90): 
 1. days 2 and 3: the reserve fixtures for 3 days ahead (0x54c5b0 + 0x7e6380: push &date; mov ecx, [0xb74434] -> thiscall, ret 4) and, on day 3, also for tomorrow; 
 2. the fixture news queue ([+0x1128], a list): each news item goes to the manager of the club in slot 0 if slot 0xe asks for it and to the manager of the club in slot 1 if slot 0xf asks for it (0x785830: push k; mov ecx, news -> thiscall, ret 4; 0x7861e0: push club; push news; mov ecx, [0xb7431c] -> thiscall, ret 8); the list is destroyed (0x68d040 + 0x944c94) and [+0x1128] becomes 0; 
 3. days 5 and 6, if yesterday is in the same year: in yesterday's lists (the 3 slices, the key nations up to [0xb64738]), from back to front, the friendlies ([0x9cf684], type +0x3a = 1) between two clubs without a human manager leave the list (0x68d1d0 + 0x68d280); the first fixture that is not a friendly of that type ends the list; 
 4. the leg check list ([0xae2a48]): each entry whose cup (or its stage +4) has +0x43 = 1 labels the following fixtures of the round (0x522c70: push +0xb; push +7; push round; ecx = the cup -> thiscall, ret 0xc); the list is emptied (0x68d080).

Builds the general.dat summary: the active nations (two groups), the human managers with club and nation, the game date, the version, the play time and time(). 
 `build_save_game_summary(summary)` (cdecl): the summary that `save_game_data` writes into `general.dat` (right after the version): 
 - +0: the nations of the league table (0xb63d60, 0x23 of 0x48 bytes) with bit 2 set in +0x11c, the first through sprintf with its own name as the format (0x944c9f), the others through the translated ", <%s>" (0x66f4e0); +1000 (0x3e8): the same with bit 1; 
 - 16 managers, from the last of the person table (0xae23bc, 0x6e bytes) backwards: a human one (+0x5f = 1) gives the name at +0x7e4 + 0x78 × i (0x53dba0, 200) and at +0x820 + 0x78 × i "club / nation" (+0x39 and +0x24, name at +0x38 of each), only one of them, or nothing; a non-human one only zeroes the name (the club stays as it was in the caller's buffer); 
 - +0xf64 the game date (0x417c10 of 0xae2c90), +0x7d0 the version (0x90d130), +0xf6c the play time ([0xdd7140] += time() − [0xdd7144]; [0xdd7144] = time()) and +0xf70 the time().
